// Married to Sable: Characters/Dialogue/MarriageDialogueSable. Keys follow
// vanilla's (Leah's file is the model): weather and indoor/outdoor lines,
// Good/Neutral/Bad by how the marriage is going, leaving for and coming back
// from the shop, the patio, children, and a few days of the year.
// Items in [brackets] are a little something Sable leaves for you.
{
  "Rainy_Day_0": "Rain on the roof, coffee on the stove, nowhere to be. I'm going to paint until the light gives up.$h",
  "Rainy_Day_1": "I left you some coffee. It's the good beans. Don't tell the shop's accountant. (It's me.)[(O)395]$u",
  "Rainy_Day_2": "Flat gray light. Every color tells the truth on days like this.",
  "Rainy_Day_3": "The canvases warp in the damp. I've moved them all into the kitchen. Sorry.$u",
  "Rainy_Day_4": "Don't track mud on my drop cloth. ...Actually, do. It's a good brown.$h",
  "Rainy_Night_0": "You're soaked. Sit by the stove. I'll make tea, badly, like Evelyn taught me.",
  "Rainy_Night_1": "I painted the rain on the window all afternoon. It's terrible. I'm keeping it.$h",
  "Rainy_Night_2": "Listen to it. Like someone washing brushes on the roof.$l",
  "Rainy_Night_3": "I found mud on the ceiling. I've decided not to ask.$u",
  "Rainy_Night_4": "Come here. You're the warmest thing in this house.$l",
  "Indoor_Day_0": "Good morning. There's paint on the kettle. I don't know how either.$u",
  "Indoor_Day_1": "I made you something small. Don't make a fuss.[(O)blinxxy.MuseArt_Canvas_Small (O)blinxxy.MuseArt_Pigment_rose]$l",
  "Indoor_Day_2": "The light in this house is all wrong in the morning and perfect at four. I've planned my life around four.",
  "Indoor_Day_3": "I sketched you while you were asleep. You snore in ochre.$u",
  "Indoor_Day_4": "Coffee's on. I may have used the brush water by mistake. Taste it first.$u",
  "Indoor_Night_0": "Sit still. No, like that. ...Okay, you can move. I've got your hands.",
  "Indoor_Night_1": "Ten years I didn't paint. Now I can't stop. I'm blaming you.$l",
  "Indoor_Night_2": "Evelyn says hello. She also says you need to eat more vegetables, which is rich, coming from her.$h",
  "Indoor_Night_3": "I keep looking at the pendant. I've mixed a hundred blues. None of them were this one.$l",
  "Indoor_Night_4": "Don't look in the studio corner yet. It's not finished. It's never finished. Go to sleep.$u",
  "Outdoor_0": "The light on the crops this morning... hold on, I need a pencil.$h",
  "Outdoor_1": "Your fields are a patchwork. Every square a different green. You've made a painting and you don't even know it.",
  "Outdoor_2": "Wind's from the west. The clouds will be good by noon.",
  "Outdoor_3": "Don't work yourself into the ground. I'm not painting you as a scarecrow.$u",
  "Outdoor_4": "Some of the best colors I own came from this farm.$h",
  "Good_0": "Good morning, my favorite subject.$l",
  "Good_1": "I used to think a finished painting was a failure waiting to be noticed. Now I think it's just a finished painting.$h",
  "Good_2": "You look good in this light. You look good in most light. I've checked.$l",
  "Good_3": "Hold still. You've got a smudge. ...There. Now it's a better smudge.$u",
  "Good_4": "When you came into the shop that first time, I thought you were lost. You were. So was I.$l",
  "Good_5": "I sold a painting today. One of mine. A woman from Zuzu City cried a little.#$b#I may have cried a little too.$h",
  "Good_6": "Be careful in the mines. I need you in one piece. I've only painted you in one piece.",
  "Good_7": "Thank you for ruining my quiet, empty life.$l",
  "Neutral_0": "Morning. I'm thinking about the color of toast. Don't interrupt.",
  "Neutral_1": "The shop's slow this week. Everyone's busy planting. Including you.",
  "Neutral_2": "If you're going into town, Pierre owes me for six frames.",
  "Neutral_3": "I need more umber. I always need more umber.",
  "Neutral_4": "The kitchen table is a still life now. Please don't eat it.$u",
  "Neutral_5": "Do you think a cow would sit for a portrait? Asking for no reason.",
  "Bad_0": "You haven't looked at anything I've painted in weeks.$s",
  "Bad_1": "I'm painting things that are empty again. I know what that means.$s",
  "Bad_2": "The critic was half right, you know. I'm technically flawless. Lately I'm also completely alone.$s",
  "Bad_3": "...Do you still like being here? With me?$s",
  "Bad_4": "I've started fixing other people's paintings again. It's easier than talking to you.$s",
  "patio_Sable": "Don't look yet. It's your barn at sunrise. The barn is cooperating. The sunrise isn't.$u",
  "spouseRoom_Sable": "This corner gets the north light. Every painter wants the north light. I got it by marrying a farmer.$l",
  "funLeave_Sable": "I'm going to paint by the river today. I'll be back before the light goes.",
  "funReturn_Sable": "I painted the river and the river won. How was your day?$h",
  "jobLeave_Sable": "I'm off to open the shop. Don't let the chickens near my easel.",
  "jobReturn_Sable": "Sold four canvases and a very expensive brush. I'm a magnate now. What's for dinner?$h",
  "OneKid_0": "%kid1 painted the dog. And the floor. And the dog again. I'm so proud.$h",
  "TwoKids_0": "Two little painters. The walls never stood a chance.$h",
  "spring_1": "A new year. I've bought far too many canvases for it.$h",
  "summer_1": "Summer. Everything's too bright to paint and I'm going to try anyway.$u",
  "fall_1": "Fall. My season. Try to keep up.$h",
  "fall_9": "You remembered my birthday. You always do. ...I've painted you something. It's in the studio corner.$l",
  "winter_1": "Snow on the farm. Blue in the shadows, pink in the sun. Come and look.$l"
}
